		{"id":"38ebffac768581a1","type":"text","text":"Example: terrain generation\n1. Create plane\n2. Subdivide plane\n3. Displace plane using noise\n\nOR\n1. Create cube\n2. Voxelize cube (including its volume)\n3. Assign each voxel certain noise value\n4. Remove voxels which have certain value","x":1091,"y":-918,"width":570,"height":340},
		{"id":"acf68e6918854575","type":"text","text":"Non destructive:\n* Fast development iterations\n* Algorithmical description\n","x":1078,"y":278,"width":298,"height":150,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"356d6469cdf82e84","type":"text","text":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PTVal-t9g1k","x":2151,"y":233,"width":449,"height":60},
		{"id":"5a6d046f7e4136b8","type":"text","text":"Parametric model","x":-3717,"y":-2274,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"b3c7be7693eac9b4","type":"text","text":"Inputs","x":-3717,"y":-2094,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"151ae4bb5a5c10dd","type":"text","text":"Sculpting-based modeling is sometimes better choice for 3D character creation.","x":-2422,"y":-1114,"width":809,"height":60},
		{"id":"c8905168538105ab","type":"text","text":"However, procedural modeling is great for character FX ","x":-1523,"y":-1114,"width":501,"height":71,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"0d536fc201bf893b","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/NotBestApps/sculpt.jpg","x":-2422,"y":-1052,"width":809,"height":455},
		{"id":"eeb5db23ede72696","type":"text","text":"Characters","x":-1773,"y":-1475,"width":250,"height":88,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"dc32bbf03629b5a4","type":"text","text":"Zbrush: https://www.zbrushguides.com/resources/sculpting-materials","x":-2422,"y":-597,"width":809,"height":50},
		{"id":"a11e6407ecd3cb20","type":"text","text":"Procedural modeling is maybe not the best choice for:","x":-880,"y":-1974,"width":326,"height":80,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"599b2e13a17578e6","type":"text","text":"\"No silver bullet\"\n\nProcedural modeling is usually used in combination with other modeling and rendering techniques.\n\n","x":-2260,"y":-2314,"width":484,"height":150,"color":"3"},
